Tells a window no output drew that it's suspended, and that it isn't once
an output draws it again, as xdg-shell's suspended state lets a compositor
say of a window nobody can see. niri never sent the state, so a client
that skips only suspended windows, as kitty does, kept drawing every
hidden one: on a workspace not shown, scrolled out of view or a tab
behind another. Each second the fallback timer suspends each window whose
surface no output's last frame held; a frame that holds it unsuspends it,
and it shows what it last drew for that one frame, as a window scrolled
into view already does. A window being cast is never suspended, since
its cast would freeze. The headless backend draws nothing, so its timer
suspends nothing; src/tests/suspended.rs says what each output drew.

